X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=117938910009238

I just installed OpenBSD/alpha 4.1 on the API Networks CS20 Dual 833  
MHz Alpha machine that arrived this week. On the first bootup with  
GENERIC, I had hundreds of errors stating the following:

alipm0: timeout st 0x0

These kept repeating a few hundred times and then something else in  
the boot process would load and then hundreds more. When logged in  
through ssh I don't see the error but I experience pauses of a second  
or so every few seconds. Using UKC to disable alipm(4) corrects the  
problem but I thought it was worth while to point this error out.  
This is also the case with 4.1-stable. The dmesg follows but with  
alipm(4) disabled. The only thing listed in the dmesg with alipm(4)  
enabled is the above error.

Bryan


